---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { SITE_URL, ENTITY_STATEMENT } from '../data/site.js';

const profileSchema = {
  '@type': 'ProfilePage',
  '@id': `${SITE_URL}/about#page`,
  url: `${SITE_URL}/about`,
  name: 'About Ally Madrone',
  mainEntity: { '@id': `${SITE_URL}/#ally` }
};
---

<Base
  title="About"
  path="/about"
  description={`${ENTITY_STATEMENT} This page tells the integrated story and provides copy-paste bios in three lengths.`}
  extraSchema={profileSchema}
>
  <h1>About</h1>
  <p class="kicker">{ENTITY_STATEMENT}</p>

  <img
    class="headshot"
    src="/images/ally-madrone.jpg"
    alt="Ally Madrone, a smiling bearded man in an olive button-up shirt wearing a wire-wrapped stone pendant"
    width="1200"
    height="1200"
    loading="eager"
  />

  <p class="lede">
    My career looks like a zigzag until you see the thread. Clinical research, then a farm, then
    identity verification, then content security. Every one of those is the same job: understand a
    living system well enough to protect the people inside it.
  </p>

  <p>
    I started in clinical research at Oregon Health &amp; Science University, learning how evidence
    gets made and how easily it gets contaminated. Then I went to study living systems directly,
    earning a B.S. in Horticulture on the research option at Oregon State University. In 2015 I
    founded Root Connection, a scientific research and horticultural design firm in Portland, and
    grew it to a million dollars in annual revenue over six years. Running that company taught me
    what I now do for a living: multi-stakeholder projects, technical research, and designing for
    systems that don't sit still.
  </p>

  <p>
    In 2021 I moved into identity. At Veriff I worked enterprise identity verification for financial
    institutions, learning KYC, fraud operations, and the procurement reality of regulated
    industries. At Trust Stamp I owned the deepfake detection API end to end, from writing the first
    PRD to packaging detection for financial crimes and identity fraud use cases. That work put me in
    the room where synthetic media stopped being a curiosity and became an attack surface.
  </p>

  <p>
    Since January 2025 I've been VP of Product at Deep Media, a content security infrastructure
    company. I lead product across the platform: Shield, Skills, and Guardian, spanning detection
    tools, composable workflows, and autonomous investigation agents that hunt digital harms across
    the surface, deep, and dark web. Deep Media's work is trusted by the U.S. Department of Defense
    and major technology platforms.
  </p>

  <p>
    The thread that holds all of it together is a question I've carried since the farm: how do we
    act with integrity toward the systems we're entangled with, ecological, digital, human, and
    artificial. Permaculture ethics and platform trust and safety are closer than they look. Both
    are about designing conditions where the whole system can stay healthy, instead of fighting each
    symptom after the damage is done.
  </p>

  <p>
    I live in Knoxville, Tennessee with my family. The rest of the whole person lives on the
    <a href="/garden">garden</a> page.
  </p>

  <h2>Bios for copy and paste</h2>
  <p>
    These are maintained by me and safe to use verbatim for event programs, introductions, and
    press. A speaker headshot is on the <a href="/speaking">speaking</a> page.
  </p>

  <div class="bio-block">
    <h3>Short bio (50 words)</h3>
    <p>
      Ally Madrone is VP of Product at Deep Media, a content security infrastructure company trusted
      by the U.S. Department of Defense and major technology platforms. He builds AI systems that
      detect synthetic media and disrupt fraud networks, and he speaks widely on AI-enabled
      financial crime. He lives in Knoxville, Tennessee.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="bio-block">
    <h3>Medium bio (150 words)</h3>
    <p>
      Ally Madrone is VP of Product at Deep Media, a content security infrastructure company trusted
      by the U.S. Department of Defense and major technology platforms. He leads product across Deep
      Media's platform, including autonomous AI agents that investigate fraud, disinformation, and
      other digital harms across the surface, deep, and dark web.
    </p>
    <p>
      Ally has spent his career at the intersection of identity, fraud, and trust and safety. He
      owned the deepfake detection API at Trust Stamp, worked enterprise identity verification at
      Veriff, and is a regular speaker for organizations including the International Association of
      Financial Crimes Investigators on deepfakes, synthetic identity fraud, and AI-enabled social
      engineering. Before tech, he founded and ran Root Connection, a horticultural research and
      design firm he grew to $1MM in annual revenue. He holds a B.S. in Horticulture from Oregon
      State University and lives in Knoxville, Tennessee.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="bio-block">
    <h3>Long bio (300 words)</h3>
    <p>
      Ally Madrone is VP of Product at Deep Media, a content security infrastructure company trusted
      by the U.S. Department of Defense and major technology platforms. He leads product strategy
      across the full platform: Shield, the detection and API layer, Skills, the composable
      capability layer, and Guardian, autonomous AI agents that proactively investigate fraud,
      disinformation, and other digital harms across the surface, deep, and dark web.
    </p>
    <p>
      Ally's path into content security ran through identity and fraud. At Trust Stamp he owned the
      deepfake detection API end to end, packaging synthetic media detection for financial crimes,
      KYC, and identity fraud use cases, and authoring technical responses to federal RFIs on
      synthetic identity detection and biometric liveness. At Veriff he worked enterprise identity
      verification for financial institutions, developing deep expertise in KYC workflows and the
      operational reality of fraud teams in regulated industries.
    </p>
    <p>
      He is a frequent educator on AI-enabled financial crime, speaking regularly for the
      International Association of Financial Crimes Investigators and other industry bodies on
      deepfakes, synthetic identity fraud, and AI-driven social engineering. He spoke at TrustCon
      2024 on deepfake detection, and his team FaceLock won the Safety by Design Trust &amp; Safety
      Hackathon in 2024.
    </p>
    <p>
      Before tech, Ally founded Root Connection, a scientific research and horticultural design firm
      in Portland, Oregon, and grew it to $1MM in annual revenue. He holds a B.S. in Horticulture on
      the research option from Oregon State University. The through line of his work is a single
      question: how do we act with integrity toward the systems we're entangled with, ecological,
      digital, human, and artificial. He lives in Knoxville, Tennessee with his family.
    </p>
  </div>
</Base>
